# How-To: Safely Trigger Office C2R Updates

Guide for triggering Microsoft Office Click-to-Run (C2R) updates on VDI environments without interrupting active user sessions, RPA bots, or scheduled tasks.

---

## 1. Pre-Flight Check (Active Processes & Sessions)

Verify whether any Office applications or COM-based background workers are currently active before initiating maintenance.

```powershell
# Inspect active Office processes across all sessions
Get-Process -Name WINWORD, EXCEL, POWERPNT, OUTLOOK, MSACCESS -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue |
    Select-Object Name, Id, SessionId, StartTime

# Inspect active user sessions (VDI / RDS)
quser
No output: The system is completely idle; updates apply immediately upon download.

Active processes detected: Proceed with safe staging (forceappshutdown=false) to avoid terminating unsaved work or automation workflows.

2. Trigger Safe Background Update
Execute the native Click-to-Run client. Using forceappshutdown=false downloads and stages update payloads in the local cache without killing running processes.

PowerShell
$C2RPath = "$env:ProgramFiles\Common Files\microsoft shared\ClickToRun\OfficeC2RClient.exe"

if (Test-Path -Path $C2RPath) {
    Start-Process -FilePath $C2RPath -ArgumentList "/update user displaylevel=false forceappshutdown=false"
    Write-Output "Update triggered successfully with graceful application handling."
} else {
    Write-Error "OfficeC2RClient.exe not found at target location."
}
Parameter Reference
displaylevel=false: Suppresses UI wizards, dialogues, and notifications.

forceappshutdown=false: Blocks forced app termination. The update remains staged and finalizes automatically the next time apps are closed or during the next system reboot.

3. Verification & Monitoring
Check Installed & Reported Version
Query the Click-to-Run registry tree to view the current reporting build:

PowerShell
Get-ItemProperty -Path "HKLM:\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\Office\ClickToRun\Configuration" |
    Select-Object VersionToReport, ClientFolder, UpdateChannel
Follow Real-Time C2R Engine Logs
Inspect live engine status during download and integration:

PowerShell
# Stream the latest Office C2R execution log
$LogFile = Get-ChildItem -Path "$env:WINDIR\Temp" -Filter "*Client*.log" | 
    Sort-Object LastWriteTime -Descending | 
    Select-Object -First 1

if ($LogFile) {
    Get-Content -Path $LogFile.FullName -Tail 25 -Wait
}
